    "content_for_agents": {
      "summary": "The Heptameron is a 14th-15th century magical treatise attributed to Solomon, compiled by Peter de Abano. It provides a complete system for angel invocation, exorcism, and spirit conjuration based on the planetary hours. Each hour of the day and night is governed by a planet and its corresponding angel, with specific incenses and candles for each.",
      "key_concepts": [
        "Seven planetary angels and their hours",
        "Consecration of implements by planetary correspondence",
        "Exorcism using sacred sword and divine names",
        "Conjuration within a consecrated magic circle",
        "Proper dismissal of spirits"
      ],
      "historical_context": "The Heptameron reflects the angelological tradition of medieval Christianity blended with planetary magic. Peter de Abano (1257-1316) was an Italian physician and astrologer who compiled existing magical traditions into a systematic treatise.",
      "modern_relevance": "The planetary hour system remains widely used in ceremonial magic. The angel invocation methods are foundational to Enochian magic and Thelema. The exorcism framework influenced later grimoires including the Key of Solomon.",
